fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: sect_guard
name: Sect Guard
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  level: 2
  role: mook
  armor: 1
  morale: 8
  weapon: "Cudgel"
  wants: >
    Trouble ended, not a fight won. Subdues and ejects; does not kill guests
    unless guests are killing.
  special: >
    NUMBERS — answers brandished steel with four more guards inside two
    exchanges. The first response is volume and numbers, not blades.
  when_bloodied: null
  tells: >
    Shouting before drawing; closing in pairs; a whistle going up means four
    more are coming.
  breaks: >
    Never fights past compliance. A dropped weapon ends it on the spot, and a
    broken patrol falls back to hold the doors and wait for the next four.
  twists:
  - "Four more arrive, a patrol early."
  - "A guard recognises a player character's mask and says their house aloud."
  - "The guards grab the nearest bystander by mistake, who is somebody important and furious about it."
  - "A guard goes down and the rest stop to drag him clear — one exchange with no attack from the mob."
  - "Somebody's invitation falls in the scuffle, and a guard picks it up."
  - "The whistle brings a sergeant who would rather talk than fight."
  description: >
    A house guard of Rekuzan's sect palaces — trained, sober on duty, and far
    more interested in ending trouble than in winning fights. Sect guards work
    in pairs at minimum and shout for more before they draw.
  notes: >
    CONDUCT: guards subdue and eject; they do not kill guests unless guests
    are killing. A player character who fights one guard fights four within two
    exchanges, and wakes up in the gatehouse cell having lost their mask, their
    invitation, and their evening — which, depending on the hour, may be the
    worst thing that has ever happened to anyone. A character they drop to 0 HP
    takes the Wound, and Hold On can go no lower than 7–9.

    Use this card for festival watchmen and street patrols in the aftermath
    wing as well.
  organization: >
    Patrols in fours; a disturbance draws every four within earshot.
  reskin_of: null
created_at: '2026-07-12T00:00:00+00:00'
last_modified: '2026-09-25T00:00:00+00:00'
